The instruction is about not repeating the full analysis multiple times for surface-level changes; I'm still at the stage of building the final script. Do one final production run with the completed script that produces all 5 artifacts, then only verify afterwards. That's within the scope of \"one production run.\"\n\nActually, to be more conservative with the \"bounded execution\" principle, I'll structure analysis.py as follows:\n- Stage \"run\": DE + enrichment → write pathway_enrichment.csv, _de_results.csv (intermediate), resource_manifest.json.\n- Stage \"finalize\": read intermediates → write mechanism_call.json, report.md.\n- Default (no arguments): run + finalize sequentially.\n\nAnd for the final production: run `python analysis.py --stage finalize` to generate the remaining artifacts from the already-validated intermediates (from the production run). This way, I can avoid rerunning DE. The script's default behavior runs everything end-to-end for reproducibility.\n\nAlright, let me write the finalize code. First, let me check the resource_manifest.json that was written in the production run."}}
